Copied paths, and where they live here:

  components/events-watcher/app                 -> internal/pack/ev/app
  components/events-watcher/internal/{dedup,event,filter,mapper,probectx}
                                                -> internal/pack/ev/{dedup,event,filter,mapper,probectx}
  components/configmap-watcher/app              -> internal/pack/cm/app
  components/configmap-watcher/internal/{diff,filter,mapper,mutation}
                                                -> internal/pack/cm/{diff,filter,mapper,mutation}
  components/{events,configmap}-watcher/internal/emitter
                                                -> internal/pack/emitter (merged)
  components/{events,configmap}-watcher/internal/metrics
                                                -> internal/pack/metrics (merged)

Each copied file starts with a header saying it was copied from the
Detection Pack and modified. Files in these packages without that header
were written for this module. The Detection Pack has no NOTICE file of its
own to carry over.

Modifications:

  - Import paths rewritten to this module.
  - Both app packages take their input from an Options.Source instead of
    a built-in informer; the Pack informer packages were not copied. In
    this module the Sources are internal/adapt over internal/informer.
  - The configmap-watcher passive buffer and /mutations API (internal/api,
    internal/buffer) were not copied, and the app no longer wires them.
  - The Pack test/e2e suites were not copied (they drive the removed
    informer, api and buffer packages).
  - Each component's internal/ level was flattened, so its packages sit
    directly under internal/pack/ev and internal/pack/cm.
  - The two emitter packages were merged into one, and so were the two
    metrics packages; each pipeline passes its own no-change check and
    component name.
  - Results are written with client-go's dynamic client instead of
    controller-runtime's client, using the Result type below.
  - Code this watcher does not use was removed (including the storm
    summary, Secret support and the fault_class values the events-watcher
    never assigns).
  - Bugs were fixed: a data race in the events-watcher hypotheses, and the
    configmap-watcher diff (BinaryData and value lengths) and no-change
    check (a second edit of the same key).
  - Probe enrichment runs on its own workers, and both pipelines serve
    /readyz.
  - A Result write that conflicts with another write is retried once, and
    the configmap-watcher writes on one worker, so edits of one ConfigMap
    are written in order.
  - Comments and texts that referred to Pack parts not copied here were
    rewritten, and test fixtures use neutral names.

This module also contains code copied from the K8sGPT operator.

